842 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1753 0 R
/E (Integration of Standard Hardware Extensions: Expand the instruction set architecture beyond the base RV32I profile by integrating the standard RISC-V 'M' extension. This implements dedicated hardware multiplication and division units, eliminating the latency and execution overhead of software emulation libraries for compute-heavy tasks. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
843 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1754 0 R
/E (Automated Hardware Performance Monitoring: Transition from manual, software-driven mode switches via explicit CSR writes to a fully automated hardware mechanism. Integrating an on-chip monitor to track real-time pipeline stall rates and instruction retirement metrics would allow the core to self-scale its execution depth dynamically. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
844 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1755 0 R
/E (ASIC Migration and Fine-Grained DVFS: Migrate the RTL design from programmable FPGA fabric to a standard-cell ASIC flow to eliminate high static logic leakage. Moving to custom silicon enables true Dynamic Voltage and Frequency Scaling \(DVFS\), allowing the core voltage to scale down alongside the 20 MHz clock to maximize energy savings for ultra-low-power commercial IoT applications. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
